              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ērudiō, ērudīre — \"to educate, to polish\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pater fīlium dīligenter ērudīvit. The father educated his son carefully."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ērudiō, ērudīre, ērudīvī; its participle follows in a later lesson. Ē + rudis, rough: to take the roughness out. English erudite."
            }
          ]
        },
