          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ērudiō is built from ē \"out of\" and rudis \"rough, untaught\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): to bring out of the rough state. English erudite comes from its participle."
            }
          ]
        },
