              "text": "īnstituō, īnstituere — \"to train up, to instruct; to set up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Puerōs ad virtūtem īnstituēbat. He trained the boys in virtue."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "īnstituō, īnstituere, īnstituī, īnstitūtum, in + statuō: to set up, then to set a young mind in order. Īnstitūtum is its noun."
            }
          ]
        },
