          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "īnstituō is built from in and statuō \"to set, to place\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), the vowel weakened inside the compound. English institute comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
